Romanian Pro — licences of the files in this directory
=======================================================

ro.clex, ro.cngm (and source/ro.txt)
------------------------------------
Licensed under Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0),
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

These files are adaptations (word frequencies and word-pair probabilities, filtered, merged,
quantised and encoded in the CLEX1 / CNGM1 formats) of:

  * FrequencyWords by Hermit Dave, https://github.com/hermitdave/FrequencyWords, content
    CC BY-SA 4.0 (Romanian 2018 list, derived from OpenSubtitles 2018, opus.nlpl.eu;
    P. Lison and J. Tiedemann, LREC 2016).
  * Romanian Wikipedia (articles and discussion pages), Wikiquote, Wikivoyage and Wikibooks,
    dumps of 2026-11-01, © their contributors, CC BY-SA 4.0 / GFDL.
  * Romanian Wikinews, dump of 2026-11-01, © Wikinews contributors, CC BY 2.5.
  * Tatoeba Romanian sentences, https://tatoeba.org, © Tatoeba contributors, CC BY 2.0 FR.
  * Mozilla Common Voice Romanian sentence-collector text, CC0 1.0.

Changes: text extracted from wikitext; Unicode NFC and comma-below normalisation; sentence
splitting; held-out data removed; words counted, filtered, merged with documented weights,
cleaned of diacritic-less misspellings, ranked and cut to 150,000 words; word pairs counted,
mixed, pruned and quantised. No sentence text is included. No endorsement by any source is implied.
Hunspell ro_RO (rospell) was used only as a yes/no check at build time; none of its data is included.

ro.mlmodelc, ro.bpevocab (and the identical ro_ro, mo, rup copies), when present
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

A neural next-token model (Core ML, compiled from neural/ro.mlpackage) and its subword vocabulary,
trained on the training split of the Romanian Wikipedia (articles and discussion pages),
Wikiquote, Wikivoyage and Wikibooks text (CC BY-SA 4.0 / GFDL), Romanian Wikinews (CC BY 2.5),
Tatoeba Romanian sentences (CC BY 2.0 FR) and Mozilla Common Voice sentence-collector text (CC0 1.0),
with the sources and attribution listed above. Changes: text extracted, normalised, filtered and
reduced to network weights and a byte-pair vocabulary; no sentence text is included. The model
architecture, tokenizer and Core ML conversion come from the official Clink tools/train-neural.py
(Clink Community Assets License 1.0, copied unchanged in vendor/tools/).

